    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** serving as our primary offensive anchors. **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) faces a highly favorable matchup against Elmer Rodr\u00edguez, benefiting from a soft SP_xERA of 5.31 and a significant boost from his prime #3 spot in the order. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (81.77) draws a plus matchup against Seymour, where favorable winds blowing out provide a needed cushion to offset a slightly pedestrian base projection. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** remains in a \"Lineup Pending\" status, his projected 71.94 score makes him a lock if he hits in the cleanup spot, as his platoon advantage against Baz provides a high-floor ceiling for Roto production.\n\nThe decision-making process for the final utility spots was tight, particularly regarding **Heliot Ramos** (59.48) and **Henry Bolte** (59.22). **Henry Bolte** was elevated by a massive 10% boost for his leadoff placement against Lambert, making him an essential component to our pursuit of Stolen Bases. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Sam Antonacci** (45.50); while his efficiency is lower, his inclusion is a calculated risk to maintain category depth. **Coby Mayo** (55.81) represents the most interesting marginal start; despite the dynamic platoon penalty, the extreme weakness of Rodr\u00edguez\u2019s pitching profile forces him into the starting lineup over internal alternatives like **Miguel Vargas** or **Brayan Rocchio**, who lacked the requisite matchup upside today.\n\nRisks today are concentrated on environmental and tactical variables. **Liam Hicks** (40.69) faces an elite test against Wheeler, where wind blowing in suppresses his already marginal outlook; he is a candidate for early removal if the game script turns sour. Furthermore, the reliance on assumed lineups for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos** creates a volatility window\u2014should they be shifted out of their respective #4 and #3 holes, their efficiency scores will likely drop toward the \"Below floor\" threshold. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remaining sidelined, our depth is thin, placing the burden of production squarely on our core veterans to carry the weight while we wait for prospects like **Jacob Wilson** or **Franklin Arias** to provide late-season utility.",
